{
    "reasoner_response": "Let the customer know: "I can see you have a 2022 FORD EXPLORER XLT on file. To start a new claim, I'd recommend beginning with your selling dealer, John Halt Motors, who can be reached at 3123560000. They're familiar with your contract and can work directly with Assurant on your behalf. If you prefer another repair facility, your contract may require you to return to your selling dealer. To confirm, you can view your contract and acceptable repair locations at vehicle care plan dot com. The repair facility—not you—must contact Assurant to initiate and authorize the claim process before any repairs begin. Here’s how it works: 1) Take your vehicle to a repair facility (selling dealer preferred, or any location found on vehicle care plan dot com), 2) The repair facility contacts Assurant to get the claim authorized, 3) Assurant reviews and authorizes covered repairs. By the way, you can quickly view claim status, manage your contract, find answers to frequently asked questions, or chat with Customer Care at vehicle care plan dot com. Is there anything else I can help you with?",
    "communication_rules": [
        "- If the customer tried to change the topic while you are waiting for Supervisor instructions, before following any Reasoner's instructions, ask the customer whether they want to switch to the new topic or continue with the current one.",
        "- If any previous requests were prevented from execution, they can now be re-evaluated and executed if appropriate. Make a new function/tool request to do so."
    ]
}
